Resuming

1. Set variables in Cloud Shell (they reset between sessions):

RG=soc-lab-rg
LOC=austriaeast
MYIP=


2.2. Check public IP. Look it up from your own computer. If it changed, update both rules, or SSH will hang:
az network nsg rule update -g $RG --nsg-name mgmt-nsg \
  --name Allow-SSH-MyIP --source-address-prefixes $MYIP
az network nsg rule update -g $RG --nsg-name web-nsg \
  --name Allow-HTTP-MyIP --source-address-prefixes $MYIP

3. start VMs
az vm start -g $RG -n jumpbox --no-wait
az vm start -g $RG -n elk-vm --no-wait

az vm list -g $RG -d -o table

4. Connect
ssh -i ~/.ssh/soc-lab-key azureadmin@68.210.101.27

ssh -i ~/.ssh/ansible-key azureadmin@10.0.3.4
cd ~/elk && docker compose ps


5. Reopen Kibana 
ssh -i ~/.ssh/soc-lab-key -L 5601:10.0.3.4:5601 azureadmin@68.210.101.27
Browse to http://localhost:5601.

6. Check the quota request. Before creating the web VMs, look at Quotas, Compute, Austria East in the portal. The web VMs are the next job once the limit is raised.


